      "sha256": "e2b0d262757f01c1794a938c78d32600a21e289b2a0320e5c660c4c6fc9aa87e",
      "bytes": 4056,
      "statement": "The release states that the Cepheid distance uncertainty is included in the supplied covariance; the same README describes STATONLY principally in SN terms.",
      "short_quote": "uncertainty is incorporated in covariance matrix .cov"
    },
    {
      "id": "Brout2022_v2",
      "path": ".work/unified-cosmology/calibration-interface/Brout2022v2.html",
      "url": "https://arxiv.org/html/2202.04077v2#S2.SS3",
      "sha256": "7580cd8300bf5bf53119735a06c94f7240a7426c37a4f2e8fdbf9915905ecb38",
      "bytes": 518758,
      "statement": "Equation15 adds the SN covariance and a Cepheid covariance once. It does not publish the numerical host-to-lightcurve expansion algorithm.",
      "short_quote": null
    },
    {
      "id": "Riess2022_v3",
      "path": ".work/unified-cosmology/distance-ladder/Riess2022v3.pdf",
      "url": "https://arxiv.org/pdf/2112.04510v3",
      "sha256": "572e5d2c0f32bf6e80a118eec13ed0107e1e2830f9ebe90b5bc4e9d1b7fa5df1",
      "bytes": 9544553,
      "statement": "Figure16 describes37host covariance without SN data; section5.2 proposes using that first-two-rung factor with consistently standardized SNe. Table6 distinguishes leave-one-host-SN-out and all-SN-free means.",
      "short_quote": "derived only from the first two rungs and without the use of any SN Ia data"
    },
    {
      "id": "Scolnic2022_v2",
      "path": ".work/unified-cosmology/calibration-source-review/Scolnic2022v2.pdf",
      "url": "https://arxiv.org/pdf/2112.03863",
      "sha256": "c42406c774a1f09ba520238b4bbe6bbcba81fec6171fdf0064d7c4dca583b9c9",
      "bytes": 3331484,
      "statement": "Section3.1 finds no evidence for a shared intrinsic SN distance residual among siblings; section3.2 shares intrinsic scatter among repeated observations of the same SN. This distinction does not remove their common Cepheid distance.",
      "short_quote": "no covariance should be given for measurements of SN distances in the same galaxy"
    },
    {
      "id": "pipeline",
      "path": ".work/unified-cosmology/calibration-source-review/PPLUS.yml",
      "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PantheonPlusSH0ES/DataRelease/c447f0fea703fcd0fff57de5000947b5ca81286b/Pantheon%2B_Data/7_PIPPIN/PPLUS.yml",
      "sha256": "869ee1b5fdeedfdcde094e5162355322e9fe00eec5010ea2aed81ef1993050d8",
      "bytes": 142395,
      "statement": "Lines4126-4133 list external duplicate-scatter and peculiar-velocity inputs; NOSYS selects DEFAULT+DUP_SIGINT. The active blocks do not specify the later Cepheid-covariance expansion into the public file.",
      "short_quote": null
    },
    {
