  "findings": [
    "Four distinct-SN sibling blocks reproduce shared STATONLY covariance 1.97248-1.99790 times the independently reconstructed SN-free host variance.",
    "A single uncertain shared host distance contributes one host variance to each sibling covariance: Cov(m_i-u,m_j-u)=Cov(m_i,m_j)+Var(u) when the SN and host measurements are independent. Two siblings do not themselves imply twice that term.",
    "The paper-level model and source data do not establish which exact host covariance, version, mapping or additional term built the released arrays. A doubled embedding, another release version, and an undocumented additional term cannot be distinguished by the inspected public evidence.",
    "The README label STATONLY is not a guarantee of a diagonal or Cepheid-free matrix. Do not add a second Cepheid factor to the released matrix or subtract the independently reconstructed factor and declare an exact SN-only covariance.",
    "Preserve the official released joint likelihood as a conditional route. An independently rebuilt likelihood needs the exact SN-only covariance and original host-to-row expansion/mean construction, or a full from-observable reconstruction."
  ],
